{"created": "2026-09-15T13:21:46.102713+00:00", "modified": "2026-09-15T13:52:53.502701+00:00", "id": 22770065, "conceptrecid": "22421850", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22770065", "conceptdoi": "10.5281/zenodo.22421850", "doi_url": "https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22770065", "metadata": {"title": "Replication package: Who Gets the House? Financing-Associated Price Gaps in New York City", "doi": "10.5281/zenodo.22770065", "publication_date": "2026-09-15", "description": "<p>Replication package for <em>Who Gets the House? Execution Certainty, the Mortgage Recording Tax, and the Design of Transfer Taxes in New York City</em> (Pablo Loschi).</p>\n<p><strong>Source code, documentation, and live updates on GitHub:</strong><br><a href=\"https://github.com/pgold30/who-gets-the-house\" rel=\"noopener\">https://github.com/pgold30/who-gets-the-house</a></p>\n\n\n<h3>Quick Start</h3>\n<pre><code>git clone https://github.com/pgold30/who-gets-the-house.git\ncd who-gets-the-house\nbash run_all.sh\n</code></pre>\n<p><em>(Or download and extract <code>03_replication_package.zip</code> from this deposit). Executes Stages 1 to 3 in about four minutes. Requires Python 3.9+ and numpy.</em></p>\n<h3>Replication Stages</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Stage 1 &mdash; Arithmetic Audit:</strong> Internal consistency verification requiring no external data or network, re-deriving all 170 stated manuscript quantities directly from primitives.</li>\n<li><strong>Stage 2 &mdash; Headline Estimates:</strong> Offline reproduction of the headline repeat-sales estimates from the included analysis panel and Department of Buildings permit microdata.</li>\n<li><strong>Stage 3 &mdash; Heterogeneity &amp; Mechanism:</strong> Full replication of the corporate/individual buyer identity split and real-estate-owned (REO) foreclosure analysis of Section 4.9.</li>\n<li><strong>Stage 4 &mdash; Raw API Rebuild:</strong> Complete end-to-end pipeline rebuilding the analysis panel directly from public NYC Open Data and CFPB HMDA endpoints.</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Data Sources</h3>\n<p>All inputs are public, free, and require no proprietary license or key:</p>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>NYC Department of Finance:</strong> Annualized Calendar Sales (<code>w2pb-icbu</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>ACRIS Real Property:</strong> Master (<code>bnx9-e6tj</code>), Legals (<code>8h5j-fqxa</code>), Parties (<code>636b-3b5g</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>ACRIS Personal Property (Co-ops):</strong> Master (<code>sv7x-dduq</code>), Legals (<code>uqqa-hym2</code>), Document Codes (<code>7isb-wh4c</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>NYC Department of Buildings:</strong> Permit Issuance (<code>ipu4-2q9a</code>)</li>\n<li><strong>CFPB:</strong> Home Mortgage Disclosure Act (HMDA) Data Browser API</li>\n</ul>\n<h3>Licensing</h3>\n<ul>\n<li><strong>Code:</strong> MIT License</li>\n<li><strong>Derived Data &amp; Documentation:</strong> Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0)</li>\n<li><strong>Source Data:</strong> Public domain (City of New York &amp; CFPB)</li>\n</ul>", "access_right": "open", "creators": [{"name": "Loschi, Pablo", "affiliation": "Independent researcher, Berlin"}], "keywords": ["transfer taxes", "mortgage recording tax", "execution certainty", "bunching", "repeat sales", "New York City", "ACRIS", "housing"], "version": "v2.0", "references": ["Loschi, P. (2026). The Execution-Certainty Wedge: Allocation, Distribution, and the Design of Housing-Market Instruments (Version 3.1). Zenodo. https://doi.org/10.5281/zenodo.22770434"], "custom": {"code:codeRepository": "https://github.com/pgold30/who-gets-the-house", "code:programmingLanguage": [{"id": "python", "title": {"en": "Python"}}], "code:developmentStatus": {"id": "active", "title": {"en": "Active"}}}, "resource_type": {"title": "Software", "type": "software"}, "license": {"id": "cc-by-4.0"}, "relations": {"version": [{"index": 1, "is_last": true, "parent": {"pid_type": "recid", "pid_value": "22421850"}}]}}, "title": "Replication package: Who Gets the House? Fin